      },
      "text": "The Islamic Golden Age (~750-1258 CE) was not merely a transmission belt passing Greek knowledge to medieval Europe. Islamic scholars actively transformed, corrected, and extended the Greek heritage across mathematics, optics, medicine, astronomy, and chemistry."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-ISLAMIC-GOLDEN-AGE.md#003",
      "path": [
        "02-ISLAMIC-GOLDEN-AGE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
